# The Nest API this app reads.
#
# Copy to `.env.local`. It is read at BUILD time, not at request time: the app is
# `output: "export"` (see next.config.ts), so `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined
# into the bundle by the compiler. Two consequences worth knowing before a demo:
#
#   1. Changing this requires restarting `npm run dev`, and pointing a deployed
#      build at a different API requires a rebuild and a redeploy. It is not a
#      runtime setting.
#   2. `localhost` is meaningless in a deployed build — it resolves to the
#      visitor's own machine. A deployment needs a reachable hostname.
#
# Unset, every API call fails with "The API could not be reached" rather than
# silently resolving against this site's own origin and parsing an exported HTML
# page as JSON. Screens show their error state and say so.
#
# The API defaults to port 3000 and so does `next dev`, so they cannot both take
# it. Give the API another port when you start it (`PORT=4000 pnpm start:dev` in
# the AdvisoryPlatformAPI repo) and point this at that.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
